# The build stage compiles the sources itself, so the host's build output
# (build/, 54 MB) and Gradle caches must never reach it. BuildKit only sends
# the paths named by the COPY instructions (build scripts, gradle/, src/main/),
# so today these rules do not change the context; they keep the image
# independent of the host if a broader COPY is added, and they apply to
# builders that send the whole context (legacy builder, Buildah/Podman).
# The tests do not run in the image, so their sources are excluded as well.
.gradle/
build/
.kotlin/
src/test/
src/integrationTest/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.log
